If the number of records passed to mapper is too low, it will not get the optimal results.

I thought I could return keyval(NULL, NULL), it goes wrong with it.

When I run the code against the whole data set(1.4Gb). The boundary problem ocurrers( Well, it's not a problem for other algorithms). The last instance of mapper on the datanode may only recieve a somall number of records(<100), and it's bad for apriori with large column numbers(>1000). So, I just skip the small tail.

When I checked the log file of the job, it says it got 1000 transactions to process for the mapper instance.
It will be great if I can control how many records fed to mapper each time.

Thanks.

Chao

